            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If your business relies on hauling temperature-sensitive goods, investing in a new reefer trailer is one of the most important decisions you can make. These trailers are critical for keeping products fresh and safety compliant – from produce and pharmaceuticals to floral shipments and frozen goods.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "But when you’re searching for a <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer&condition=new\">new reefer trailer for sale</a>, it’s not just about picking something that looks good on the lot. It’s about finding equipment that delivers consistent performance, matches your workload, and won’t let you down when timing and temperature matter most. Before you make your next big purchase, here are five things to keep in mind.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-hauling-requirements",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "1. Know Your Hauling Requirements",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "hauling-requirements"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-hauling-requirements-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Start with the basics: What kind of freight will you be moving, and how far will it need to travel? Different loads require different temperature ranges. Some products, like ice cream or seafood, demand ultra-low temperatures, while others, like pharmaceuticals or dairy, need to maintain a precise and steady climate.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-hauling-requirements-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Choosing a <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer\">reefer trailer</a> that’s engineered for your specific freight can help you avoid energy waste, product loss, or compliance issues down the road. If you’re unsure which specs you need, your trailer dealer should be able to guide you through the right fit.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-insulation",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "2. Consider Insulation and Construction",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "insulation"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-insulation-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Even the most powerful reefer unit won’t perform well if the trailer’s insulation isn’t up to par. Look for high-quality insulation and durable construction that can withstand the wear and tear of regular loading and unloading. The floor, walls, and ceiling should all be built to maintain cold air, reduce thermal leaks, and prevent water intrusion.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-insulation-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Insulation isn’t just a performance factor—it directly affects your bottom line. Better thermal protection means your reefer unit doesn’t have to work as hard, saving you fuel and reducing wear over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-fuel-efficiency",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "3. Don’t Overlook Fuel Efficiency",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "fuel-efficiency"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-fuel-efficiency-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Fuel costs can eat into your margins faster than you think, especially when running long hauls. New reefer trailers generally offer improved fuel economy over older models, but make sure to ask about the specific fuel consumption of the unit you’re considering. Look for models with automatic start/stop features, programmable temperature cycles, and aerodynamic trailer designs that can help cut down on drag and improve mileage. Over the course of a year, those small savings add up.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-compliance",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "4. Look for Compliance with Regional Standards",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "compliance"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-compliance-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you operate in Florida, it’s important to make sure your <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer\">reefer trailer</a> meets all applicable state and federal transportation standards. In Florida, you need to ensure your trailer complies with DOT safety regulations, weight limits, and refrigeration performance standards—especially when transporting perishable goods. If you’re crossing state lines, additional compliance requirements may apply depending on your route.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-compliance-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A good dealer won’t just sell you a trailer—they’ll help ensure it’s cleared to operate legally and efficiently across Florida and beyond, giving you peace of mind before you ever hit the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-dealer",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "5. Buy From a Dealer You Can Count On",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "dealer"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-dealer-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When you’re looking for a <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer&condition=new\">new reefer trailer for sale</a>, who you buy it from is just as important as what you buy. A reputable dealership will help you find the right match for your business, walk you through the specs, and provide service and support long after the sale.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-dealer-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we believe in more than just equipment—we believe in partnerships. We take the time to understand your needs, recommend the right solutions, and offer ongoing support so you’re not left figuring things out alone. With us, you get more than a trailer. You get peace of mind, backed by experience and service you can trust.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-move-forward",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Get What You Need to Move Forward",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "move-forward"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-move-forward-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Finding the right <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer&condition=new\">new reefer trailer for sale</a> is about more than checking boxes—it’s about making a smart investment for your business. From the refrigeration unit to the dealer relationship, every detail matters when you’re transporting temperature-sensitive products. Whether you’re expanding your fleet or upgrading your equipment, <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a> is here to help you make the right call. Our team is committed to making sure you get exactly what you need, with honesty, professionalism, and unmatched customer care. Ready to talk <a href=\"/store/inventory?type=trailer\">reefer trailers</a>? <a href=\"/contact\">Stop by or give us a call. We’ll help you find the best fit for your business.</a>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
